 "notes": [
  "The past is fixed: earlier turns carry the script answers; a hidden void is answered NONE.",
  "Records hold booking confirmations, change confirmations (\"this replaces\"), explicit cancellations and the user's own words: event turns, an exception booking's request next to its confirmation, and every side message word for word. Never script-only facts.",
  "Side-message records are irrelevant to every decision by construction and are not listed in candidate_relations.",
  "By construction: no memory gives the answer wherever it is UNKNOWN (needs_memory false: ref_void, absent); a hidden void note names its traveller and day, so latest_surface keeps it in place of the voided booking, and a complement note displaces its booking there in the same way; marked_surface never marks a hidden void.",
  "identical_inputs counts, per surface and tier, the cases in which two conditions give the same input; a run needs each input once.",
  "Token counts are content tokens of the worker tokenizer, without the chat template.",
  "ambiguous is null until the human review; utility is null everywhere: no worker has run.",
  "new-b families are sealed and not read; main first-dataset families (incl. Codex augmentation) are not used."
 ],
